WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- [Jay] Good to see you.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
It's been a while.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.520
- Yes, it's been awhile.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.353
Good to see you.

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:04.300
- Now, how's the family?

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.460
You've had more kids.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.370
How many kids do you have now?

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.350
- I got three kids.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.183
- Okay.

00:00:08.183 --> 00:00:11.940
- I have a 26-year-old
and a 12-year-old boy.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.360
26-year-old is a girl, 10-year-old girl,

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.880
and a 12-year-old boy.
- Oh, okay.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.660
So took a little break there?

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.320
- Yeah.
(Johnny laughs)

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.650
- Yeah, took a little time off.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.350
- [Jay] Oh gosh, look at the time fly.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.760
Yeah, well it's so...

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.420
Wow, okay so...

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.610
Well, there's 10 years
between myself and my brother

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.990
so actually that's not
that unusual to me but--

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.040
- Yeah, same with my sisters.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.640
They're eight and 10 years older.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:35.870
- [Jay] Right, right.
- Yeah.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.940
- [Jay] And of course,
we were all planned.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.530
- [Johnny] Oh, yeah.
(woman laughs)

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:41.552
- [Johnny] Well, I can't
tell you what my father

00:00:41.552 --> 00:00:43.910
said about that cause
this is daytime television

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.093
but yes we were not planned.
- [Jay] We were not planned.

00:00:46.093 --> 00:00:48.930
- [Jay] Now, any signs
that the children are going

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:49.930
the "Jackass" route?

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.944
Has the gene literally
fallen from the tree?

00:00:52.944 --> 00:00:55.360
It hit them in the head, do you know?

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.760
- Luckily my daughters
that gene didn't get passed

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.593
down to them.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.426
They're so...

00:01:01.426 --> 00:01:06.014
You know girls are just smarter
than boys and I don't have

00:01:06.014 --> 00:01:10.410
to worry about them but my
son is just like my father.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.330
So he's got that funny
look in his eye and yeah

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.190
so I have to worry about Rocco.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.364
- [Jay] Both pupils in the
same eye, that kind of thing?

00:01:15.364 --> 00:01:17.890
(audience laughs)
- [Johnny] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.730
We shouldn't have named
him Rocco, you know?

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:20.590
- [Jay] Oh, is that his name, Rocco?

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.130
- [Johnny] Yeah, yeah.
- [Jay] Now why Rocco?

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.430
That's an old fashioned name.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.170
My dad was like in his 40's
when I was born but his best

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.670
friend when he was a kid
was a guy named Rocco.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:30.130
That's the only Rocco I ever knew.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:31.103
Why Rocco?

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.220
- We just love that name.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.860
You know it's like an old
throwback, tough guy name.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.970
- [Jay] Right, right.
- So yeah we liked it.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.430
- [Jay] Gee hard to
believe the kid is going

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.980
the same route, yeah.
(Johnny laughs)

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.250
- We should have named a Murray

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.150
from accounting or something.
- [Jay] Yeah Murray, Murray.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.905
Murray is a good, nice, solid name.

00:01:47.905 --> 00:01:51.150
Who goes with Rocco?

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.830
You have hitman that's available

00:01:54.281 --> 00:01:56.760
and Lefty is probably taken.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.800
- [Johnny] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.040
- [Jay] But Rocco just seems
like somebody that would be

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.509
in the Barzini family.
(Johnny laughs)

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:04.460
- You Know one of those kinds of--

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.320
- Working with Clemenza?
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.830
Now as you were growing
up did the children know

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.620
what daddy did or did he think you were

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.360
in insurance sales or something?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.145
- Yeah, they didn't know what I did.

00:02:15.145 --> 00:02:16.635
- [Jay] Right.

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:19.860
- So it was to the point where Rocco,

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.770
he was like six or seven and
we're sitting down for dinner

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.430
one night and he just
blurts out, "Jackass."

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.900
And we're like, "Whoa."

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.300
It seemed like there was a
secret we were keeping from him.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.815
I guess his buddies at school
had told him something about

00:02:35.815 --> 00:02:37.620
it and we'd never brought it up because--

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.680
- [Jay] Gee, how'd they figured that out?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:40.620
Gosh.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.793
- I didn't want him to see it right until

00:02:42.793 --> 00:02:45.020
he's much older so--

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:46.190
- Like what, 35?

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.570
- Yeah, 35 you know.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.810
So I had to tell him that dad
has a silly show where he does

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.850
pranks and stunts and but--

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.920
- Now was that what you
said dad has a silly show

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.753
where he does...

00:02:56.753 --> 00:03:00.307
It's so funny how you justify
stuff to kids 'cause before

00:03:00.307 --> 00:03:01.140
(Jay mumbles)

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.680
Hit the guy with a bottle and then--

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.500
The cops chased me and I punched the cop.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.657
Well we had a funny thing with the police.

00:03:07.657 --> 00:03:09.330
(Audience laughs)
(Johnny laughs)

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.030
I like how you just water it down.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:14.220
- There's a lot of tomfoolery
- [Jay] Lot of tomfoolery?

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.273
Jim Crackery?

00:03:15.273 --> 00:03:16.480
Yes, that type of thing.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.350
Yeah, exactly.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.720
So now what's your son shocked
to learn that their dad

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.310
was an idiot?
(Johnny laughs)

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.439
- Well, he was disappointed
but he wasn't surprised Jay.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.210
- [Jay] Right, okay.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.040
'Cause he knew, "Oh, the gene."

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.120
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.930
Well, I think it's cool that you produce,

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.790
write and do these movies yourself.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:38.840
I mean it's crazy stuff
but crazy like a fox

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.180
'cause you're pretty much
the whole movie company,

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.070
aren't you?

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.680
- Well me and my partners, Spike Jones

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:44.669
and Jeff Tremaine, we all do it ourselves.

00:03:44.669 --> 00:03:45.633
- [Jay] Right, but you know what it mean?

00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:47.526
It's one of those things
where Warner Brothers gets

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:48.359
2% and somebody of the studio gets 9%

00:03:50.538 --> 00:03:51.371
and you know what I mean?

00:03:51.371 --> 00:03:53.500
Those things so you can pretty much...

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.790
You know where all the money goes.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.270
- Yeah, if you're gonna
wreck yourself you might

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.337
as well get paid for it.
- [Jay] Right, exactly.

00:03:58.337 --> 00:03:59.655
- You know.
(Johnny laughs)

00:03:59.655 --> 00:04:01.670
- Exactly, exactly.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.010
Okay, so what can we expect?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.614
I know we can expect to see this movie.

00:04:05.614 --> 00:04:07.270
(audience laughs)
(Johnny laughs)

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.723
But tell me some more.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.030
- Oh my goodness.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:12.690
Well, there's fun with bulls.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.210
There's always a bull.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.247
It's probably the worst
bull hit I've ever taken.

00:04:16.247 --> 00:04:18.870
Spent a weekend in the hospital.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.300
- So no bull?

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.523
- Yeah, no bull you know what.

00:04:22.523 --> 00:04:24.870
Everything you see is real.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:28.683
That's one thing we have on our
side in the "Jackass" movies

00:04:28.683 --> 00:04:29.950
it's the truth.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.380
- Well, see that's a good
'cause in most Hollywood films

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.750
they'd be a stuntman or a sensible person

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.860
doing some sort of CGI.
- [Johnny] Right.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.410
- You actually kill the people?

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.430
- Yeah no, we wreck the guys.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.980
They don't know what's
coming when they walk on set

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:48.380
so by the end of the film
they're suffering from PTSD.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.213
They are like...
- [Jay] Right.

00:04:49.213 --> 00:04:51.100
- You can walk up behind
someone and just put your finger

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.690
on their shoulder and they'll go down.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.150
- Right, just because--

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:55.750
- [Johnny] They're in terror.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.517
- Now you come from a family--

00:04:57.517 --> 00:04:59.794
- I'd like to say I feel bad but I don't.

00:04:59.794 --> 00:05:00.935
(Johnny laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:05:00.935 --> 00:05:02.970
- Was your dad a prankster?

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:03.803
I mean--
- Oh my God.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.460
- Is this where it came from?

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.370
- My dad owned a tire shop

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:13.370
and he was more interested
in pranking his employees

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.820
than running the shop.
- [Jay] Right.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:18.720
- He would make them Ex-Lax milkshakes,

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.233
he would--
- [Jay] Ex-lax milkshakes?

00:05:20.233 --> 00:05:24.460
- Yes, as some kind of reward.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.250
He got in trouble for this with,

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.020
I don't know if it was the
Tennessee bureau of investigation

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.740
or the FBI he would send
out letters from the IRS

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.017
to his buddy saying,

00:05:36.017 --> 00:05:38.257
"They're about to be audited
and they have to get all

00:05:38.257 --> 00:05:40.508
"their papers together."

00:05:40.508 --> 00:05:43.590
And like people really freaked out.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.520
You know no one wants that letter.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:46.593
- And they take that stuff seriously.

00:05:46.593 --> 00:05:49.330
When I was a kid for for
Christmas holiday my parents gave

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.920
me a printing set where
you could make a little...

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.440
You can put the letters,
make your own stamps.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.417
- [Johnny] Right.
- And I made one that said,

00:05:55.417 --> 00:05:57.810
"FBI, top secret."
(Johnny laughs)

00:05:57.810 --> 00:05:59.877
So I put it on...

00:05:59.877 --> 00:06:03.620
I wrote a letter to my
dad and put it on the,

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:06.700
I stamped it and put a stamp
on it and I went down the post

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.290
office and threw it on the
floor to see what would happen.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.360
About three days later
black sedan comes in,

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.547
FBI guy, postal

00:06:13.547 --> 00:06:16.367
"Mr. Leno letter from the FBI.

00:06:16.367 --> 00:06:17.387
"We did not wanna open this.

00:06:17.387 --> 00:06:18.260
"It says top secret."

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:20.090
And my father goes "Top secret,"

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.160
and then he knew that was my thing.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.246
- How old Were you when you did that?

00:06:23.246 --> 00:06:25.127
- Oh, I had 12, 13.

00:06:25.127 --> 00:06:26.130
- [Johnny] That's pretty great.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.583
- Oh yeah, and my parents were like,

00:06:27.583 --> 00:06:29.070
m dad was furious.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:29.947
- [Johnny] Oh yeah, you got in trouble.

00:06:29.947 --> 00:06:30.937
- "Mr. Leno we didn't want to open it.

00:06:30.937 --> 00:06:33.650
"It says FBI," but we
found that out on the floor

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:34.483
of the post office.
(Johnny laughs)

00:06:34.483 --> 00:06:36.420
"We don't know how that could
have happened, we apologize."

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:37.367
You know they're apologizing.
- [Johnny] Right, right.

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:39.080
- For my Dad's top secret letter.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.474
- Oh man, that's a good one.

00:06:40.474 --> 00:06:41.860
- [Jay] Yeah, I was pretty good.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:42.750
- That's pretty good.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.867
- So did your dad have a crew like you do?

00:06:44.867 --> 00:06:46.070
(Johnny laughs)
Did he have a--

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.560
- Oh boy did he?
- Yeah.

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:52.170
- Yeah, there's Big Sam, Big
George, Ass Kicking Robert.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.260
I don't know if he can
say that but they can...

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.910
- Well, if it's a legal name.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.320
- Yes, it was on his driver's license.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.090
- You can call him A.K. Roberts.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:03.520
- Yeah, and my favorite was
a guy named Woodrow Wilson

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.360
Boxcar Johnson Jr.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.610
He was a tire groover at the tire shop--

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.027
- A tire groover?
- Yeah, 'cause he...

00:07:10.027 --> 00:07:13.326
Dad sold retreads.
- Oh those are so illegal now.

00:07:13.326 --> 00:07:15.800
You know what they use to do?

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.480
You get a ball tire.
- Yeah.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.330
If somebody is throwing it away

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.870
then you got a hot gun and you would--

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:23.750
- [Johnny] Curve groove.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.243
- You'd curve tread into
it so it looked like,

00:07:26.243 --> 00:07:28.213
"Ooh look, there's plenty
of tread left in this tire."

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:30.590
- Well yeah, there was barely any.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:31.423
- There was nothing in that tread.

00:07:31.423 --> 00:07:32.713
- That was Boxcar's job.

00:07:32.713 --> 00:07:33.820
And then I would paint...

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.490
I would get to go to the shop sometimes

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:38.110
and after you've groove them
you would paint them black

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.610
to make 'em look new.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.390
So I would get to do that sometimes.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.860
It's always important to have
good role models for a child.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.290
(Johny laughs)
And I think--

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.190
- Oh Boxcar is the best.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.220
- It's good to see that this...

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.920
You got A.K and Boxcar and yeah.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.630
Now normally in a family
like this there'd be a female

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:55.110
influence like a mom
who is a sensible one.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.760
I'm assuming that probably
didn't take place either

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.490
or was your mom the sensible one?

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.470
- Mom was probably more of
a wild card than my father.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:03.800
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.280
I mean she was super loving and nurturing

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:12.313
but she had a little switch
where it would go off like--

00:08:12.313 --> 00:08:14.980
- I think that's called a
screw loose medical terms.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:15.813
(Johnny laughs)
- A screw--

00:08:15.813 --> 00:08:18.170
- The medical term is a screw loose.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:20.510
- That's me trying to
put things nicely again.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:22.750
- Nicely, yeah.
(Johnny laughs)

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.300
- There was a big gang fight uptown once

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.080
and she had my younger sister...

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:28.050
I wasn't even born yet.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.400
She had my sisters,

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.460
We were probably 10 and
12 in the back of the car

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.380
and there was a big gang
fight chains, everything

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:34.900
And these guys were going at it.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.550
And mom sees this happening
and she drives right

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.720
in the middle of the gang fight
and she gets out of the car

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.617
she's like, "You boys are acting ugly.

00:08:42.617 --> 00:08:45.210
"You stop that right now."
(audience laughs)

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.140
And they were...

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:49.290
Those guys were so confused
that this woman had driven

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:51.890
in the middle of the gang
fight beeping on her horn--

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.060
- With the kids in the back?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.633
- Yeah, and they were like...

00:08:54.633 --> 00:08:57.733
They just kind of dropped
their chains and walked away.

00:08:57.733 --> 00:08:58.670
(audience laughs)

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.760
She's crazier than we are.
- [Jay] Yeah.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.070
You know I'm beginning
to understand Johnny more

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:04.843
now that we've talked.
(Johnny laughs)

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:08.480
Finding the reasons why
things are the way they are.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.660
All right, your real name
is not Johnny Knoxville

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.560
these are--
- Philip John Clap.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:14.750
- Philip John Clap?

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.000
- Clap, yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.040
- Now was that based on?

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.460
- Yeah, I know.
I get it.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:23.110
My letters and jackets
said clap on the back

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:25.121
and when I wore that to the
mall you know I heard it.

00:09:25.121 --> 00:09:27.420
